{"results":[{"url":"https://www.factcheck.org/issue/obamacare/","final_url":"https://www.factcheck.org/issue/obamacare/","title":"obamacare Archives - FactCheck.org","description":null,"language":"en","text":"An ad from a Democratic-aligned super PAC claims Republican Sen. Dan Sullivan “voted to raise Alaskans’ healthcare costs by $1,800 and on that same day voted to give himself a $500,000 taxpayer-funded payout.” But that’s not the whole story, and the ad leaves the false impression that Sullivan received that money.\n\nElon Musk and the Department of Government Efficiency have been tasked by President Donald Trump with slashing federal spending. But social media posts falsely claim that as part of that effort, DOGE stopped “royalties” to former President Barack Obama related to the Affordable Care Act, known as Obamacare. The claim came from a satirical website.\n\n### Biden’s Factual Distortions\n\nFormer Vice President Joe Biden distorted the facts in two interviews in the wake of the Nevada caucuses, claiming Sen. Bernie Sanders “was opposed to Obamacare” (Sanders voted for it) and that Biden never labeled South Carolina as his campaign’s “firewall” (he did).\n\n### ‘Broke’ and Because of ACA?\n\nHouse Speaker Paul Ryan falsely claimed that “because of Obamacare, Medicare is going broke.” The law actually improved Medicare’s financing, and the program isn’t going “broke.”\n\n### More Bogus Trumponomics\n\nDonald Trump mangled his economic facts — again — when he said many people are working two jobs largely “because of this horrible Obamacare.”\n\n### Rubio’s Shaky ACA Hypothetical\n\nSen. Marco Rubio described a hypothetical Detroit business owner with 10 employees as facing higher costs under the Affordable Care Act, saying the man was considering moving one employee to part time to “save … a significant amount under Obamacare.”\n\n### Obama’s Numbers (April 2015 Update)\n\nJobs, earnings, health insurance, oil production, exports and more. Our latest installment of the Obama scorecard.\n\n### Father Doesn’t Always Know Best\n\nA super PAC formed by the father of Rep. Ted Yoho’s primary challenger claims Yoho is “first in line” at “feeding at the special interest trough,” but offers up two misleading examples.\n\n### Measuring Merkley’s Record\n\nAn ad from a Koch-backed group labels Oregon Sen. Jeff Merkley an ineffective leader because he “wrote only one bill that became law” in six years. This claim betrays a fundamental misunderstanding of the ways of Congress.\n\n### Misleading Michigan GOP Primary Voters\n\nThe Republican candidates in Michigan’s 4th Congressional District entered the final weeks of the primary trading misleading claims in TV ads that rely on deceptive tactics to distort the facts.","author":null,"published_date":null,"latency_ms":794.1905950001455,"format":"markdown"}],"errors":[]}